   "body": "### Capture result (mac/capture-batch, run 9, PR #400)\nCorpus ids: `W64x`, `W64`, `R95j`, `R95k`, `R96c`, `W65`, `R96d` (thread `fixture-test-2` between the operator's two accounts, created for this run).\n- Legacy's body (`MPListView.swift:131-150`) with a wrong `hash_check`: the 99-byte plain text \"Une erreur est survenue lors de l'envoi des données…\" (same as `W17b`), nothing deleted.\n- With the right token: link-less `.hop` \"Action effectuée avec succès\", 1 s refresh to the MP list, no cookie set. The thread leaves **only the deleting account's** list: the owner's list is empty (`R95j`) and the thread answers \"Ce message ne vous est pas destiné\" (`R96c`), while the recipient still lists it (`R95k`) until it deletes it too (`W65`, same answer; `R96d`).\n\nPublic/private actions sent (all private MP, UTC 2026-11-02): new MP 07:39:51 (`W61`), replies 07:40:58 (`W62`) and 07:41:52 (`W63`), delete with a wrong token 07:42:33 (`W64x`), delete 07:42:47 (`W64`), recipient delete 07:44:00 (`W65`). Nothing of the thread is left on HFR.\n\nChanges: LOT-094 (#186) can classify the answer (success = this sentence; the 99-byte text = bad token) and must say the thread stays for the other party; LOT-127 (#218) likewise. Facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §3.1 and §6b \"MP thread delete\".\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
